    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0512" n="472" xml:id="pg472"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">780.5/1–2654: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 184<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in
                        Pakistan</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d184-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-01-27T15:24:00-05:00">January 27, 1954—3:24
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>592. Situation reported ur 561<anchor n="2" xml:id="d184-f2"/> of greatest
                    concern here. Feel our position somewhat compromised with both Turks and Paks in
                    view of unfortunate leaks and press speculation. Amount of time involved in
                    working out complicated matters with Turkey has been surprisingly short and
                    should have been acceptable except for the press speculation. Although we feel
                    committed to Turkey that next approach to Paks should be by them, believe it
                    best that you have further frank discussion with Paks without waiting for Turks
                    if you feel this would help. You can use as much as you desire of information in
                    recent cables but should caution that much of information will be relayed by
                    Turks on matters in which they and Pakistan will have primary responsibility,
                    and that we believe it important approach come from Turkey in order that
                    consultative arrangement may clearly originate within area.</p>
                <p>Pakistan Ambassador here as well in embarrassing position and plan therefore
                    discuss situation with him along above lines today.</p>
                <p>Byroade wishes his personal and sincere
                    regrets relayed to Gholem Mohammed and PM over
                    manner in which situation has developed. He believes time has been utilized
                    profitably to work on matters which are in line with their thinking and have
                    been carried out in manner entirely acceptable but for lack of secrecy that
                    unfortunately developed. Nothing has been finalized during this period of
                    preparation nor can it be without willing agreement on all aspects by Pakistan.
                    Hope situation will now develop very rapidly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
